# Logs
logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*

node_modules
dist
dist-ssr
*.local

# Verification harness (boards/project-backlog/25-in-browser-verification-harness.md):
# built separately from `dist/` so a concurrent `npm run build` can't clobber
# a running verification pass, plus its screenshot output.
dist-verify
verify/output

# npm run dev:chrome (boards/project-backlog/110-local-dev-workflow.md):
# CRXJS dev-mode output and the dev session's own persistent Chrome profile.
# Both deliberately separate from dist/, dist-verify/ and .chrome-profile/ so a
# dev loop and a verification run can be going at once without touching each
# other's files.
dist-dev*
.chrome-dev-profile*

# npm run launch (boards/project-backlog/32-launch-chrome-with-extension-script.md):
# dedicated, persistent Chrome profile so the unpacked extension can be
# loaded outside your default profile without losing logins/settings
# between runs.
.chrome-profile

# npm run verify (boards/project-backlog/46-verify-harness-on-chrome-for-testing.md):
# Chrome for Testing, resolved/installed via @puppeteer/browsers and cached
# here so repeat runs don't re-download it.
.chrome-for-testing

# Paraglide i18n codegen (boards/project-backlog/100-paraglide-i18n-toolchain.md,
# decisions/37-i18n-paraglide.md): generated from messages/{locale}.json by the
# Vite plugin on every build and by `npm run compile:i18n` from `postinstall`,
# so a fresh clone type-checks before it builds. Paraglide emits its own
# `.gitignore` into that folder — this entry is here so the tree is DISCOVERABLE
# as generated without opening it, not because it is load-bearing.
src/paraglide

# Editor directories and files
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea
.DS_Store
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.sw?
